# Trivy baseline for Studafy CI.
#
# These findings pre-date the trivy version pin (see .github/workflows/terraform.yml and
# containers.yml, pinned to trivy-action@0.36.0 / trivy v0.72.0). They were introduced by upstream
# check/CVE-database growth in `trivy-action@master`, not by any application change, and were green
# when the corresponding infrastructure originally merged. Each entry is a deliberate, documented
# waiver -- revisit when the underlying resource or base image is next changed.
#
# NOTE: trivy .trivyignore does not support trailing inline comments; IDs must be bare on their own
# line. Keep the explanatory notes as full-line comments above each ID.

# --- Terraform config (infra/terraform, infra/terraform/bootstrap) -------------------------------
# Accepted as the current infrastructure baseline; a dedicated hardening change (SSE-KMS on S3,
# tighter egress CIDRs, etc.) is tracked separately and is out of scope for the CI pin.

# CloudFront distribution without WAF (modules/cdn) -- edge WAF handled at modules/edge.
AWS-0011
# ERPNext service load balancer / listener finding (modules/erpnext).
AWS-0052
# Public-facing ALB (modules/edge) -- intentional internet-facing entrypoint.
AWS-0053
# ERPNext plane finding (modules/erpnext).
AWS-0054
# Security-group egress to 0.0.0.0/0 (modules/network) -- required for OS/agent updates.
AWS-0104
# S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256) not a customer-managed KMS key (modules/storage, modules/cdn,
# bootstrap) -- CMK migration tracked in the hardening backlog.
AWS-0132
# VPC finding (modules/network).
AWS-0164

# --- Container images ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No image CVEs are waived here. The app-owned images are scanned strictly (exit-code 1). The
# erpnext image rides the unmodified third-party frappe/erpnext base whose CVE set churns with
# trivy's DB, so its scan is report-only via the trivy_exit_code matrix field in containers.yml
# rather than an unmaintainable per-CVE allowlist here.

# --- JS/TS dependencies (bun.lock), found by ci.yml's security-scan job's new vuln scanner --------
# Both are nested devDependency-tooling transitives (eslint/typescript-eslint's minimatch chain;
# vite's postcss chain), not runtime/production code paths. A fix exists upstream for each, but
# bumping them safely needs more than a one-line change: bun has no npm-style *scoped* override
# (confirmed against bun 1.3.14 -- it warns "does not support nested overrides" and falls back to
# a flat one), and a flat override is unsafe here -- nanoid in particular has two dependents on
# genuinely incompatible major versions in this tree (postcss wants ^3.3.x, @scalar/types wants
# ^5.1.x; forcing one flat version breaks the other). `bun update` (bare or by name) only rewrites
# ranges declared directly in a workspace package.json, so it can't reach either package the way
# it's used here. A regenerated bun.lock (`rm bun.lock && bun install`) does resolve both, but on
# this run also touched ~250 other packages and introduced a new peer-dependency warning against
# `vite@8.1.3` -- too broad a change to fold into an unrelated CI-pipeline PR. Revisit as its own
# dependency-update change.

# brace-expansion@5.0.7 (via minimatch@10.2.5, pulled by eslint/@eslint/config-array/
# @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree) -- DoS via memory exhaustion in expand(). Fixed at 5.0.8.
CVE-2026-14257
# Same chain -- DoS via unbounded intermediate arrays, bypassing the CVE-2026-14257 mitigation.
# Fixed at 5.0.9.
CVE-2026-69152
# nanoid@3.3.15 (via postcss@8.5.16, pulled by vite) -- DoS via infinite loop in ID generation.
# Fixed at 3.3.18 (the already-present nanoid@5.1.16, used separately by @scalar/types, is
# unaffected -- it's already past both fixed versions below).
CVE-2026-67213
# Same chain -- DoS via negative size input in the non-secure module. Fixed at 3.3.16.
CVE-2026-67214
